# HOST-WIDTH regression lock (Phase 9). A fixed-array size above 2^31 must survive
# the compiler's own storage intact. The size travels Tok.ival (int64_t, since the
# constant folder was widened) -> the `fixn` local -> ArrType.size -> the
# element-count diagnostic, and every one of those was a host `long` before Phase 9.
# On an ILP32-hosted tychoc that truncated SILENTLY and fail-OPEN:
# `[4294967297]int` emitted `v[1]` where LP64 emitted `v[4294967297]`, and
# `[3000000000]int` wrapped negative and died "length must be positive" instead.
#
# The goldens pin the digits, so re-narrowing the size slot shows up as a diff
# rather than as silence. A count mismatch is the vehicle deliberately: it prints
# the size through the "%lld" path twice without the program ever having to
# allocate 3e9 ints, and BOTH compilers reject it (the diag lane is differential).
fn main():
    a: [3000000000]int = [1, 2, 3]
    println(str(a[0]))
